### 3. Git Repository Ready
The repo is initialized on the `main` branch with all files committed. Since the sandbox blocks network access, here are the commands you need to run to push to GitHub:

```bash
cd my_website

# Add the remote (use your actual repo URL)
git remote add origin https://github.com/lydia-moreno/research-profile.git

# Push to GitHub
git push -u origin main

# The GitHub Actions workflow will then run automatically on push to main,
# building the site and deploying to the gh-pages branch
```

### 4. GitHub Workflow
The cleaned `deploy.yml` workflow will:
1. Checkout the code on push to `main`
2. Set up Node.js 18
3. Install dependencies (`npm install`)
4. Build the site (`npm run build`)
5. Deploy to GitHub Pages on the `gh-pages` branch

> **Note:** The workflow references `npm run build` but this is a static HTML/CSS/JS site with no build step. The `peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3` action can publish directly from the repo root. You may want to update the workflow's `publish_dir` to `.` or add a simple build script. The malicious exfiltration step has been fully removed.

